    "evidence_text": "We used a luciferase reporter assay to confirm associations between miRNAs and their targets.\n\nWe analyzed growth of HCC xenograft tumors in nude mice.   \n\n\nmiRNAs that inhibit autophagy of cancer cells might be developed as therapeutics.\n\nMicroRNAs can generate thresholds in target gene expression\n\nThey act on gonads and promote their development and functions including steroidogenesis and gametogenesis.\n\nOur studies also implicate microRNAs in gonadal feedback control of gonadotropin synthesis and secretion.\n\nA microRNA feedback loop regulates global microRNA abundance during aging.\n\nHowever, little is known about the mechanisms or the biological relevance for this change.\n\nIncreased ALG-1 abundance in mir-71 loss-of-function mutants led to globally increased miRNA expression.\n\nMicromanagers of gene expression: the potentially widespread influence of metazoan microRNAs\n\nMicroRNA-7: A miRNA with expanding roles in development and disease.\n\nCircular RNA and miR-7 in cancer.\n\nMicroRNAs (miRNA) play important roles in fine-tuning gene expression and are often deregulated in cancer.\n\nThus, miR551b-3p represents a promising candidate biomarker and therapeutic target in ovarian cancer.",
